```exsecutor
interfacies Contabilis {
    functio numera(x: u32) -> u32
}

publica functio f(x: dyn Contabilis) -> u8 {
    redde 0;
}
```

`dyn Contabilis` is a trait object. `dyn Trait poscit {P}` narrows the trait's declared ceiling at the cast site, and the row is braced in type position. The reserved word `dyn` is the one English abbreviation among the Latin words, kept because it is the established term.

