`externus("C", abi: sysv_amd64) { ... }` opens a foreign block with an explicit ABI; the admitted ABIs are `sysv_amd64`, `aapcs64` and `lp64d`. A raw pointer `*T` requires `Crudum`, so the foreign signature declares it. Non-atomic `refero` may not cross the boundary (`EXS-E0520`).

