}
```

`interfacies Name { ... }` declares the member signatures; `interfacies Name in T { ... }` implements them for `T`. A trait's declared rows are a ceiling on every implementation, checked at each implementation head: an implementation whose capability mark exceeds the trait's is `EXS-E0510`. Here neither declares a row, so the implementation may draw nothing.

