    redde f(v);
}

functio duplica(x: u32) -> u32 {
    redde x * 2;
}

publica functio usus() -> u32 {
    redde applica(21, duplica);
}
```

```exsecutor
publica functio imprime_gutenbergio(s: Scriptor, t: textus) -> mensura poscit sicut s {
    redde s.scribe(t);
}
```

The row is deliberately not `poscit archivum`. The authority comes from the writer that was handed in, so the function requires exactly what its `Scriptor` requires and nothing more. Point it at a writer holding `ambitus` and it requires `ambitus`; point it at one holding nothing and it requires nothing. The function does not decide and does not have to guess.

