```

```exsecutor
publica functio initium(m: Mundus) -> u8 {
    firma a = m.ambitus();
    sub ambitus = a {
        firma s = Scriptor.ad_exitum(a);
        s.scribe("x");
    }
    redde 0;
}
```

`sub P = e;` binds to the end of the enclosing scope, and `sub P = e { ... }` is the block form, so authority can be scoped tightly instead of the rest of the function being indented. The provider `a = m.ambitus()` has the atom's own type, which is what `sub` requires.

