```exsecutor
publica functio puncta(modus: u8) -> u8 {
    discerne modus {
        casus 1 { redde 10; }
        casus 2 { redde 20; }
        aliter  { redde 0; }
    }
}
```

`discerne` selects over a scrutinee with `casus` arms. A scalar scrutinee's value space is 2^N, so exhaustiveness can only be had with an `aliter` arm; without one it is EXS-E0351. Arms are blocks, there is no fallthrough, and the first matching arm wins.

Explain what this Exsecutor does and why it is written this way:

```exsecutor
publica functio puncta(modus: u8) -> u8 {
    discerne modus {
        casus 1 { redde 10; }
        casus 2 { redde 20; }
        aliter  { redde 0; }
    }
}
```

```exsecutor
typus Modus = casus ordinata, casus arborea(mensura);

publica functio valor(m: Modus) -> mensura {
    discerne m {
        casus ordinata { redde 1; }
        casus arborea(n) { redde n; }
    }
}
```

A variant can carry a payload, `casus arborea(mensura)`, and the matching arm binds it: `casus arborea(n)`. The binding is scoped to its arm. `mensura` is the target's `usize` — the type of sizes and indices.

Explain what this Exsecutor does and why it is written this way:

