    mutabilis i: u64 = 0;
    dum i lt n terminus 1000 {
        s = s + i;
        i = i + 1;
    }
    redde s;
}
```

```exsecutor
publica functio summa_ad(n: u64) -> u64 {
    mutabilis s: u64 = 0;
    per i in 0..n {
        s = s + i;
    }
    redde s;
}
```

`per i in 0..n` is the ordered loop: iteration k may observe iteration k-1. `0..n` is a range (`..`, level 6 in the precedence table) and `i` takes the range's element type, here u64 because `n` is u64. Contrast `quisque`, which declares the iterations independent.

